Role of OLAP
OLAP (Online Analytical Processing) is used to analyse large amounts of data from different
points of view, on a data warehouse that stores historical data.

 • Multidimensional analysis. Results can be viewed by dimensions such as subject,
   semester and student.

 • Roll-up and drill-down. Roll-up shows the overall result, drill-down goes down to
   individual students.
 • Slice, dice and pivot. View one subject or one semester, compare selected groups, and
   rotate the view.
 • Fast summaries. Average marks subject-wise or semester-wise are returned quickly.
 • Decision making. Compare performance across semesters, find weak subjects and top
   performers, and plan teaching support.
